            "review_title": "Review at Silk 99 Saigon",
            "review_text": "Misis N\n1 contribution\n0\nExcellent food and good service in a delight setting.\nApr 2015 • Couples\nWe had dinner at the restaurant and decided on a set menu. The restaurant was not busy and the entree arrived at our table in a short time. The entree consisted of roasted pork, BBQ pork and roasted duck. All 3 item were very tasty and perfectly cooked. The next dish was hot and sour soup, one of the best I have eaten. This was followed by pan fried fish fillet with sweet corn sauce and steamed broccoli. A very nice combination that worked well. The next dishes arrived in a very short time. It was chinese geen vegetables with assorted eggs (duck egg, century egg, quail egg and sea urchin egg) and served with fried rice with dried scallops. Desert was a plate with fresh fruit, pineapple, watermelon and dragon fruit. All fruits were very fresh and well presented. Every dish was extremely good and the staff were very attentive and obliging to our needs. First class food and service.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 7, 2015",
